module tasks.`2026-11-21-parallel-run-flakes`

task ParallelRunFlakes {
  title "Parallel full-suite flakes: provenance twenty_commit_rebase (Git temp file ENOENT/EINVAL) and projection_ownership_real_io (shutdown timing)"
  verify $ for i in 1 2 3; do make test-parity || exit 1; done
  paths "crates/bbt-mux"
  brief """
    Our stand: find the shared cause; never retry, quarantine or widen a window to hide it.

    ## Evidence
    - `bboxy450-term-mux::it provenance::twenty_commit_rebase_keeps_control_requests_responsive`: `git commit -am` -> "unable to create temporary file: No such file or directory" (inbox landing 2026-11-20 19:14, `crates/bbt-mux/tests/provenance.rs:55`) and EINVAL (full-suite candidate `1e23b5207`, 2026-11-21 ~17:00). The fixture's own temp repository loses files mid-test.
    - `bboxy450-term-mux logic::ownership_tests::projection_ownership_real_io_survives_cancel_restart_and_root_aba`: shutdown timing under the parallel `make test-parity` (2,895/2,897), passes serially.
    - Logs: `~/mydev/bbx-gate-repairs/target/ci-local.log`, `target/suite-handoff/`.
    - Leaked `dream_read.rs` supervisors (`dq1-*` temp homes, tasks/2026-11-20-test-process-leaks) keep running after their test and may operate on recycled paths; check whether either flake correlates with them or with any test that deletes shared temp space.

    ## Do
    Find the cause (shared temp paths, a test removing another's directory, a leaked process, fd/temp exhaustion); fix it at the source; prove with three consecutive green `make test-parity` runs. Run long commands detached (`nohup ... &`), one full gate machine-wide.
    ## Oracle amendment, 2026-11-21 22:30: watcher shutdown
    - Cause accepted: logic teardown blocks 6.564 s in `Worker -> Workspace -> FileWatch -> FsEventWatcher::stop -> pthread_join` (`target/fixture-handoff/mux-stack-41824.txt:447`) after an 8.792 us bus shutdown. The provenance Git flake passed in parity and 4/4 targeted runs after `42dac19c3`; record it as cured by that commit unless it recurs.
    - Granted: `crates/bboxy450-term/tests/formal_contracts/logic_worker_model.rs`, `verification/contracts.toml`, `verification/corpus.toml`. Retire the watcher off the owner thread with the existing off-owner retirement path (no new thread pool or daemon); update the logic-worker model with a broken control that joins on the owner and must violate the shutdown-progress property. Then the three consecutive green `make test-parity` runs.

    ## Oracle ruling, 2026-11-22 03:00: land the flake fix now
    - `fe4a3723d` fixes both flakes (watcher stop off the owner; Git bootstrap), passes all 2,900 parallel tests and 990 native/TLC models. The only full-run failure, `test-real-sessions`, reproduces on landed `42dac19c3` and is unrelated: two saved Python cards in the Oracle's own session log (`01M7VC8QBWY7P55AVTX648HXKJ.jsonl`: one cancelled run, one moved-to-background run) render without a status. Moved to [[tasks/2026-11-22-python-card-status-shapes]].
    - **Do:** `make land` `fe4a3723d` (detached, one gate). The "three green test-parity runs" criterion is replaced by: full `make test-parity` green except `test-real-sessions`, named. Report with the task verify command and its real exit.


    ## Report from seat:01M7ZVK9YFPRSBR7EJF6DPC5E1

    Landed both MUX flake fixes at signed e05c4c21194c229c501a8fc076ef786603ecd4e4. Detached make land exited 0 with 437 MUX tests and 992 native/TLC models on the landed source. The full gate passed 2,900 parallel tests and 990 models on the equal pre-rebase patch. The parity loop exited 1 at the Oracle’s amended test-real-sessions exception, reproduced on landed baseline 42dac19c3. Removed the owner-thread watcher join, repeated loose Git fixture writes, temporary tracing, and the redundant contract registration.

    ```json
